 "interpretation": "The lights of the Dipavali festival symbolize the dispelling of the darkness of ignorance and the devotee's joyous readiness for the advent of the Supreme. The devotee decorates not only the physical world with lamps, but opens all levels of their being before Him: the heart (hṛdi), the mind (mana), and the subtlest sphere of contemplation and inspiration (bhāvaloka). The Lord enters with silent footsteps, in the ever-renewing forms of divine play (līlā), filling the aspirant's being with cosmic rhythm, music, and spiritual vibration (spandan), which awakens the soul from its slumber.",
